        "finalMessage": "I fixed both issues (1 and 2) in `hmr.ts:323` by rewriting the comment. I didn't do the work the TODO asked for.\n\nThe TODO asked for `prunePaths` to also run each module's dispose callback. Doing that would change what the code does at runtime, which your rules don't allow. Upstream Vite did make that change later, but it also made `prunePaths` `async` and changed its signature, so it's a design decision rather than a lint fix.\n\nI replaced the TODO with a plain note about how the code currently behaves:\n\n```ts\n// Only their prune callbacks run here; their dispose callbacks are not triggered.\n```\n\nThat keeps the information while removing the marker both rules flag, and nothing else in the file changed. A search of the file finds no other TODO markers. There's no linter installed in this directory, so I couldn't re-run Ultracite to confirm.",
